  {
    "id": "EQ2-03",
    "question": "A P1 incident involves personal data exposed through an API. What are the response, containment, regulatory-notification, and reporting requirements?",
    "top_score": 0.6148404325571428,
    "top_vector_score": 0.602833271,
    "top_keyword_score": 0.6428571428571429,
    "top_section": "INCIDENT RESPONSE POLICY",
    "retrieval_seconds": 0.38152635500591714,
    "answer_seconds": 4.389502752994304,
    "total_seconds": 4.771056821991806,
    "answer": "- **Response:** Engage the incident response team within **15 minutes**. P1 API incidents must also be acknowledged within **15 minutes**.\n- **Containment:** Contain the incident within **1 hour**.\n- **Regulatory notification:**\n  - Notify the GDPR supervisory authority within **72 hours** because personal data is involved.\n  - Notify affected individuals **without undue delay if the risk is high**.\n  - State breach-notification deadlines vary by jurisdiction, from **14 to 90 days**.\n  - If financial data is involved and the requirement applies, notify the **SEC/FinCEN within 30 days**.\n- **Internal reporting:** Email **security@acme.com** or call the 24/7 Security Hotline at **1-800-555-CERT**.\n\nSources: **INCIDENT RESPONSE POLICY**; **SLA AND UPTIME**.",
