  {
    "id": "EQ2-06",
    "question": "What steps are required before approving a high-risk vendor that handles personal data and transfers it outside the EEA?",
    "top_score": 0.5578385866,
    "top_vector_score": 0.568340838,
    "top_keyword_score": 0.5333333333333333,
    "top_section": "THIRD-PARTY VENDOR MANAGEMENT",
    "retrieval_seconds": 0.3529410060000373,
    "answer_seconds": 3.2315996590041323,
    "total_seconds": 3.584592002996942,
    "answer": "Before approval and engagement, the following steps are required:\n\n- The business owner submits a Vendor Request Form in ServiceNow.\n- Procurement reviews commercial terms and pricing, including SLA, insurance, and liability.\n- Security conducts an assessment using a standardized questionnaire\u2014SIG Lite or CAIQ, depending on criticality.\n- Legal reviews the data processing agreement and contract terms.\n- Because the vendor handles personal data, the DPO reviews and approves the DPA.\n- Because the vendor is classified as High risk, the CISO signs off.\n- For the transfer outside the EEA:\n  - An approved transfer mechanism must be used: SCCs, an adequacy decision, or BCRs.\n  - The DPO must approve the cross-border transfer.\n- The vendor is then onboarded and added to the Approved Vendor Registry.\n\n[THIRD-PARTY VENDOR MANAGEMENT; DATA PRIVACY AND GDPR COMPLIANCE]",
