  {
    "id": "EQ2-07",
    "question": "What protections apply to a privileged administrator who works remotely?",
    "top_score": 0.4171409933571429,
    "top_vector_score": 0.534691215,
    "top_keyword_score": 0.14285714285714285,
    "top_section": "REMOTE WORK POLICY",
    "retrieval_seconds": 0.38041770400013775,
    "answer_seconds": 8.462036073004128,
    "total_seconds": 8.842488955997396,
    "answer": "A privileged administrator working remotely is covered by these controls:\n\n- **Privileged access:** Admin/root access requires MFA, follows least privilege, is reviewed and recertified quarterly, and must use individual, auditable accounts rather than shared accounts.\n- **Device and data security:** Data in transit must use TLS 1.2 or higher, data at rest must use AES-256, and the laptop must have full-disk encryption enabled.\n- **Secure use:** Security controls cannot be bypassed or disabled. Sensitive data cannot be stored on personal devices, and personal email cannot be used for business communications.  \n  *(Information Security Policy; Acceptable Use Policy)*\n\nRemote-work conditions also apply:\n\n- The workspace must be safe, ergonomic, and distraction-free.\n- Remote days require advance agreement with the direct manager; fully remote arrangements require VP approval and annual review.\n- Working outside the country of employment requires prior written approval from HR and Legal.\n- The employee must maintain core hours and meet the Slack availability requirement.  \n  *(Remote Work Policy)*\n\nUse of corporate systems may be monitored and audited in accordance with applicable law and with reasonable notice. Employee personal data is also subject to ACME\u2019s stated data-protection rights and retention rules.  \n*(Acceptable Use Policy; Data Privacy and GDPR Compliance)*",
