  {
    "id": "EQ2-08",
    "question": "Compare the operational recovery plan for Tier 1 systems with the backup schedule and backup region.",
    "top_score": 0.5806548270090909,
    "top_vector_score": 0.556779623,
    "top_keyword_score": 0.6363636363636364,
    "top_section": "BUSINESS CONTINUITY AND DISASTER RECOVERY",
    "retrieval_seconds": 0.49066518001200166,
    "answer_seconds": 2.773966744003701,
    "total_seconds": 3.2646585869952105,
    "answer": "For Tier 1 systems:\n\n- **Operational recovery objectives:** Restore service within **4 hours (RTO)**, with no more than **1 hour of data loss (RPO)**.\n- **Backup schedule:** Database backups run **hourly incremental** and **daily full**.\n- **Backup region:** Backups are stored in the geographically separate AWS region **us-west-2**.\n- **Recovery validation:** Backup restoration is tested **quarterly**. Full failover drills occur **annually**, with tabletop exercises **twice per year**.\n\nThe hourly incremental schedule aligns with the Tier 1 one-hour RPO, while the four-hour RTO defines the target for restoring operations. [BUSINESS CONTINUITY AND DISASTER RECOVERY]",
